exllamav3 1.5.1 (wheel exllamav3-1.5.1+cu128.torch2.10.0) - DFlash2 batching fix.
Without this, two overlapping requests on the DFlash2 path both crash with a
'.view()' error on a non-contiguous slice. Adds .contiguous() to the state and
logits slices passed to walk_block.
Apply from the env's site-packages folder:  git apply <path>/dflash2-contiguous.patch

diff --git a/exllamav3/architecture/dflash2.py b/exllamav3/architecture/dflash2.py
index b4df8bd..8d897c1 100644
--- a/exllamav3/architecture/dflash2.py
+++ b/exllamav3/architecture/dflash2.py
@@ -282,7 +282,7 @@ class DFlash2Model(Model):
         # (draft's last block) and the logits (target's head) may sit on other devices than
         # the selector: to_device bounces pairs with a broken peer path through the host
         out, confidence = self.selector.walk_block(
-            to_device(state[:, 1:], dev), to_device(logits[:, 1:], dev), anchor,
+            to_device(state[:, 1:].contiguous(), dev), to_device(logits[:, 1:].contiguous(), dev), anchor,
             return_confidence = export_conf,
             vocab_size = target.config.vocab_size,
             scale = self.config.output_multiplier,
